; A storey whose contents are summed against something other than its own
; outline, and over something less than all of them.
;
; The question this fixture is about is the one an appraisal asks: do the living
; rooms of this floor add up to the gross living area somebody stated? Neither
; half of it can be asked of a whole floor. The storey's outline is the living
; rooms plus the garage, so the outline is the wrong figure by exactly the
; garage; and a garage is a Space in the same way a bedroom is, so no rule about
; kinds can leave it out.
;
; Every storey below shares one set of outlines, so the shapes are the same in
; every case and what differs is the figure the sum is judged against and the
; set it is taken over. That is deliberate: the failures here are about what was
; compared with what, and holding the geometry still is what makes those the
; only variables.

; The floor plate, ten by eight, and the two cuts through it: one at x = 6 which
; separates the living rooms from the garage end, and one at y = 5 which divides
; that end into the garage and the back room.
(vertex geom:V-01 (label "Plate, south-west corner") (frame frame:building)
  (position (value (0.0 0.0 0.0) m) (source "Interior control set IC-01, Acme Surveys")
    (method method:total-station) (accuracy (independent 0.004 m)) (date "2026-02-18")))
(vertex geom:V-02 (label "Plate, south-east corner") (frame frame:building)
